The Tsurugi clearly *ought* to be useful; it's a weapon that dishes out
Cruel Brutal Damage, *and* brutally fillets people one time in twenty.

In the past, it was a pretty nice weapon; it meant giving up
lifesaving/magical breathing (because you couldn't get reflection *and*
MR *and* lifesaving while wielding a two-hander; silver DSM has changed
that), but it dished out cruel brutal damage and brutally filleted
people.

In 3.1.3 it was utterly obscene, of course (especially since in 3.1.3,
you could dispense with reflection if you had AC -18 or better) because
its descriptor defined it as doing double damage.

Now?  Twoweaponing Excalibur and a katana dishes out more damage (*much*
more once you've enchanted them up).  Cursed two-handers stop you using
all sorts of utility items.

